# Refactored Food Ordering Features Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the refactoring of the food browsing, cart management, and order placement features to strictly follow the project's established patterns: **Service Layer for logic, thin Controllers, and `asyncHandler` in Routes.**

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - Logic will be moved from Controllers to Services in `src/services/`.
> - Controllers will be refactored to remove `try/catch` and `next(error)` calls.
> - `asyncHandler` will be applied at the **Route** level, matching the `auth` pattern.
> - Zod Validators will be added and applied via the `validate` middleware.

## Proposed Changes

### [Services]
Create service files to handle business logic and database interactions.

#### [NEW] [food.services.js](file:///home/mvrck/workspace/digital-kitchen/src/services/food.services.js)
- `fetchAvailableFoods()`
- `fetchFoodById(id)`

#### [NEW] [cart.services.js](file:///home/mvrck/workspace/digital-kitchen/src/services/cart.services.js)
- `getCartForUser(userId)`
- `addItemToCart(userId, foodId, quantity)`
- `removeItemFromCart(userId, foodId)`
- `emptyCart(userId)`

#### [NEW] [order.services.js](file:///home/mvrck/workspace/digital-kitchen/src/services/order.services.js)
- `createOrderFromCart(userId, deliveryAddress)`
- `fetchUserOrderHistory(userId)`
- `fetchOrderById(userId, orderId)`

